   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Status of Implementation Progress: The business and financial model for the sustainable operation of the IFI, along with the strategy note for establishing an endowment fund, will be finalized by the selected partners in the upcoming quarter. The IFI will primarily generate revenue through fees from short, medium, and long-duration programs, with additional income from consulting services. Cash flows will be managed through program revenues, gap funding, and working capital infusions from institutions. Projections from the selected consortium indicate that IFI (CS03) will achieve financial viability and self-sustainability by the end of its fourth year. This financial stability will reduce external reliance while generating a consistent surplus, which can be reinvested in resources to stay at the forefront of technological advancements, maintain relevance, and attract top talent. This ongoing cycle of attracting high-quality faculty and increasing student engagement will ensure the IFI&apos;s long-term sustainability.

The process of establishing a Section 8 company limited by guarantee, named INNOVATRIX FOUNDATION,&apos; under the Companies Act, 2013 (18 of 2013), has been initiated by the consortium. The registration process is expected to be completed by Q2 2025.

The contract for the construction of the IFI Building was signed on April 22, 2024, officially marking the beginning of the project. Construction work officially commenced on May 1, 2024, which set the stage for the project&apos;s overall timeline.

Excavation work, up to the foundation level, was successfully completed by July 2024. This milestone paved the way for the initiation of the foundation works in September 2024, a crucial step in the construction process.

The foundation works are progressing smoothly, with a particular focus on the raft foundation. Due to the substantial size of the foundation, it has been divided into three parts for efficient execution. Part 1 of the raft foundation has been fully completed, while Parts 2 and 3 are currently under construction.

Further work is also underway on Pour 1, which includes essential structural elements such as the retaining wall, columns, and shear walls. These components are crucial for stabilizing the building and ensuring the continued advancement of the project.

The Lease Deed was executed with the Developer on 10 September 2024, for a 5-year term. The leased space has been divided into two equal sections: one designated for the institute and the other for the incubator and accelerator. Transit campus was inaugurated on 17 January 2025.</narrative>
    </title>
